      "side": 1,
      "message": "FYI: This produced a performance regression, because we inadvertently altered the sizing heuristic. In the common case, the old code would set the new reserve to:\n\n  (count + 4) + (count + 4)/4\n  \nThe new code changed that to:\n\n  count + (count + 4)/4\n  \nFor small sizes, this often only increases the capacity by 1 or 2, yielding N^2 work for a series of push-back calls. I\u0027m not going to revert - I\u0027ve got a fix-forward that should still be overflow-safe:\n\n  https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/577203",
